# This is the file Vite uses for a plain `npm run build` (default "production" mode).
# It MUST always match frontend/.env.worker's value — both point the staff app at the
# same live backend. This used to point at an old Railway deployment
# (backend-production-c487.up.railway.app) that is no longer the real backend — the
# actual backend has been on Render since the migration (see backend/DEPLOYMENT.md).
# Any build made with the old value called a dead/wrong host and every request failed
# with "Failed to fetch", which is exactly the bug this fixes. If the backend URL ever
# changes again, update BOTH this file and .env.worker together.
VITE_API_BASE=https://jsm-logistics-backend.onrender.com/api
